mail-archiver (1.3.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The token refresh unit works on installations whose data directory is
    not the default: it starts through /usr/libexec/mail-archiver-oauth-refresh,
    which takes the settings of mail-archiver.service.
  * The refresh unit can store a token in a user-owned directory (system
    accounts); the timer is enabled at the first installation only.
  * Both wrappers take the service's settings through the new
    /usr/libexec/mail-archiver-env (values with spaces or quotes were lost)
    and stop when the settings cannot be read.
  * Removing the package stops and disables its units (new prerm).
  * install-tls-cert.sh no longer logs "write error: Broken pipe" at start,
    and a passphrase-protected key file no longer hides the matching key.
  * The administrator Host page no longer answers HTTP 500.
  * Documentation: the backup command works without a drop-in directory.

 -- Madhav Diwan <madhav@decllc.biz>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:00:00 -0500

mail-archiver (1.3.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release with source packages: a source tarball, a Debian source
    package and an SRPM are built for every release.
  * search_index.py imports on Python 3.9 (it did not; EL 9 only).
  * Server-wide OAuth apps are written by administrators only; with built-in
    sign-in, administrators are the names in MAIL_ARCHIVER_ADMIN_USERS.
  * The system CA bundle is found on EL as well as on Debian.
  * See CHANGELOG.md for the release notes of this and earlier versions.

 -- Madhav Diwan <madhav@decllc.biz>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:30:00 -0500
